        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): show run failures above composer",
        "body": "Closes #108498\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users whose active Control UI run fails would see the failure rendered as an assistant transcript message. The assistant avatar, identity, timestamp, and turn styling make an operational error look like agent-authored content.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nIn this PR, the Control UI distinguishes Gateway error projections from genuine streamed or distinct terminal assistant content. It keeps real assistant output in the transcript and presents the failure in a neutral, dismissible alert aligned with the chat composer.\n\n## User Impact\n\nRun failures no longer look like agent replies or pollute the conversation. Users see the failure immediately above the composer while any genuine partial response remains visible in the transcript.\n\n## Evidence\n\n| Current behavior | Proposed in this PR |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Run failures rendered as assistant chat bubbles](https://bright-osprey-e3gj.here.now/current-behavior.png) | ![Neutral full-width run failure alert above the composer](https://coral-torque-vkd3.here.now/after.png) |\n\n- Focused UI unit tests: 307 passed.\n- Mocked Gateway Chromium E2E: 1 passed, including partial-stream preservation, transcript exclusion, placement, and width assertions.\n- Targeted formatting, lint, and `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Structured Codex autoreview: clean after addressing all accepted findings.\n- Full CI: pending on this draft PR.\n\nAI-assisted: Yes. I reviewed the complete diff, understand the behavior, and validated it with focused tests and browser evidence.\n",
